From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: map legacy AHB CALDB memory

WLAN.WBE.1.6-01270 on IPQ5332 requests a four MiB CALDB region and
requires a valid physical address before accepting calibration data.
The generic fixed-memory path returns address zero because upstream
firmware does not use cold-boot calibration, causing this older firmware
to crash during the calibration download.

For devices opting into the legacy userPD ABI, map CALDB requests to the
third reserved-memory region. Keep the existing zero-address behavior for
all other firmware.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c | 44 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -2802,13 +2802,45 @@ static int ath12k_qmi_assign_target_mem_
 			idx++;
 			break;
 		case CALDB_MEM_REGION_TYPE:
-			/* Cold boot calibration is not enabled in Ath12k. Hence,
-			 * assign paddr = 0.
-			 * Once cold boot calibration is enabled add support to
-			 * assign reserved memory from DT.
+			/* Newer firmware accepts a zero CALDB address when cold boot
+			 * calibration is disabled. Older multi-PD firmware requires
+			 * the reserved CALDB region to download calibration data.
 			 */
-			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].paddr = 0;
-			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].v.ioaddr = NULL;
+			if (!of_property_read_bool(ab->dev->of_node,
+						   "qcom,legacy-userpd-bootinfo")) {
+				ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].paddr = 0;
+				ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].v.ioaddr = NULL;
+				ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].size =
+					ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size;
+				ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].type =
+					ab->qmi.target_mem[i].type;
+				idx++;
+				break;
+			}
+
+			rmem = ath12k_core_get_reserved_mem(ab, 2);
+			if (!rmem) {
+				ret = -ENODEV;
+				goto out;
+			}
+
+			avail_rmem_size = rmem->size;
+			if (avail_rmem_size < ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size) {
+				ath12k_err(ab,
+					   "CALDB request %u exceeds reserved size %zu\n",
+					   ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size,
+					   avail_rmem_size);
+				ret = -EINVAL;
+				goto out;
+			}
+
+			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].paddr = rmem->base;
+			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].v.ioaddr =
+				ioremap(rmem->base, ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size);
+			if (!ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].v.ioaddr) {
+				ret = -EIO;
+				goto out;
+			}
 			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].size = ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size;
 			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].type = ab->qmi.target_mem[i].type;
 			idx++;
